# Force LF on files read by container shells — CRLF (which Windows git
# silently inserts on checkout when core.autocrlf=true) breaks alpine's
# /bin/sh with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M: no such file or directory".
# Symptom: ./docker-run.sh works locally on Windows; `docker exec …` of
# the same script inside a container exits 127 with a cryptic error.
#
# The rule of thumb: anything a Linux container parses (shell, Dockerfile,
# YAML loaded by a compose daemon on a Linux host) stays LF regardless
# of the developer's OS. Source files Python / Node read stay auto so
# Windows IDEs keep native line endings.
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
docker-compose.*.yml text eol=lf
